# Test the secure profile WITHOUT burning eFuses. Append after sdkconfig.secure
# (and sdkconfig.secure_esp32_legacy, if used):
#
#   idf.py -B build-secure -D SDKCONFIG=sdkconfig.production \
#          -D "SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS=sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.secure;sdkconfig.secure_virtual_efuse" set-target <target>
#
# Use a separate SDKCONFIG: an existing sdkconfig takes precedence over these overlays.
# See README.md, "Production security profile".
#
# eFuse writes go to the efuse_em partition instead of the chip. Flash contents are NOT
# protected in this mode; it exercises the boot, signing and OTA flow only. Never ship it.
# Release-mode flash encryption is unavailable with virtual eFuses, so development mode is used.
CONFIG_EFUSE_VIRTUAL=y
CONFIG_EFUSE_VIRTUAL_KEEP_IN_FLASH=y
CONFIG_SECURE_FLASH_ENCRYPTION_MODE_DEVELOPMENT=y
# HMAC reads the physical eFuse, not the virtual copy: protect NVS keys with flash encryption.
CONFIG_NVS_SEC_KEY_PROTECT_USING_FLASH_ENC=y
